ate the daimyo his  wife and children live in the capital  full-time where they serve as hostages  to ensure his loyalty but the practice  doesn't just affect the daimyo it  determines much of the rhythm of life in  Japan samurai must accompany the daimyo  to Edo this year it's been Shiraz  father's turned to go and ban Shiro is  desperate to go with him but given that  he's still in training  he'll need permission from both his  father and the domain at school and  Shiraz first lesson is in sword fighting  under his teachers Stern eye he pairs up  with his classmates and goes through the  routines  he's been practicing at the end of the  lesson he reminds the instructor of his  request to go to Edo  the instructor cracks his first smile of  the day and banter all feels confident  he will gain his support next bench ro  practices archery horsemanship and  swimming before his academic courses in  the afternoon courses cover Confucian  philosophy morality and history when the  instructor calls on him he has the  response on the tip of his tongue  ensuring another supporter for his  campaign by the end of the day and Shiro  feels confident that his formal request  will be approved but the greatest  challenge is still ahead of him  convincing his father his father  believes that martial arts are more  important than the literary arts so ban  Shiro doesn't mention his artistic  ambitions  instead he talks about renowned sword  instructors he can  and teaching certifications he can earn  to improve his professional prospects  back in Kochi then he makes his final  strongest argument if he goes this time  and succeeds his father can retire and  send him instead in the future it's this  last point that finally sells him and  Shiro's father agrees to take him on his  tour of duty in the bustle of the  capital city bank ro will finally have  the opportunity to pursue his secret  ambition to become a painter travel a  hundred and fifty years further back in  time and join forces with another group  of elite and formidable warriors the  cossacks or expand your knowledge of  japanese culture with this video on  kabuki dance drama  [Music]

